<LegalLayout title="Accessibility Statement" description="Neuhaus Foot & Ankle is working to make this website usable for everyone, including people with disabilities.">
  <p>
    Neuhaus Foot &amp; Ankle wants everyone to be able to use this website, including people with disabilities.
    We work to follow the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Use clear headings, links and labels so screen readers can read pages.</li>
    <li>Give images a text description where they carry meaning.</li>
    <li>Make the site usable with a keyboard.</li>
    <li>Use readable text sizes and strong color contrast.</li>
    <li>Make pages work on phones, tablets and computers.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Known limits</h2>
  <p>
    Some content comes from other companies, such as online booking, the patient portal and bill payment. We do not
    control those services, but we ask their providers to keep them accessible.
  </p>

  <h2>Need help?</h2>
  <p>
    If you have trouble using any part of this website, or you need information in another format, please tell us.
    You can always book or ask questions by phone, and every office can help you in person. We will work with you
    to give you the information or service you need.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
